{"repo": "python-poetry/poetry", "pull_number": 11175, "instance_id": "python-poetry__poetry-11175", "issue_numbers": ["11174"], "base_commit": "d4e6333b5577d1c13c0b3580dd6cfc3141a2faff", "patch": "diff --git a/src/poetry/console/commands/source/add.py b/src/poetry/console/commands/source/add.py\nindex 8dccbcf88fb..61eec7606be 100644\n--- a/src/poetry/console/commands/source/add.py\n+++ b/src/poetry/console/commands/source/add.py\n@@ -75,7 +75,15 @@ def handle(self) -> int:\n             )\n             priority = Priority.PRIMARY\n         else:\n-            priority = Priority[priority_str.upper()]\n+            try:\n+                priority = Priority[priority_str.upper()]\n+            except KeyError:\n+                self.line_error(\n+                    f\"<error>Invalid priority '{priority_str}'. Must be one of:\"\n+                    f\" {', '.join(p.name.lower() for p in Priority)}.</error>\"\n+                )\n+\n+                return 1\n \n         sources = AoT([])\n         new_source = Source(name=name, url=url, priority=priority)\n", "test_patch": "diff --git a/tests/console/commands/source/test_add.py b/tests/console/commands/source/test_add.py\nindex ad1487321db..735390927f1 100644\n--- a/tests/console/commands/source/test_add.py\n+++ b/tests/console/commands/source/test_add.py\n@@ -105,6 +105,17 @@ def test_source_add_error_no_url(tester: CommandTester) -> None:\n     assert tester.status_code == 1\n \n \n+def test_source_add_error_invalid_priority(\n+    tester: CommandTester, source_one: Source\n+) -> None:\n+    tester.execute(f\"--priority=bogus {source_one.name} {source_one.url}\")\n+    assert (\n+        tester.io.fetch_error().strip()\n+        == \"Invalid priority 'bogus'. Must be one of: primary, supplemental, explicit.\"\n+    )\n+    assert tester.status_code == 1\n+\n+\n def test_source_add_error_pypi(tester: CommandTester) -> None:\n     tester.execute(\"pypi https://test.pypi.org/simple/\")\n     assert (\n", "problem_statement": "`poetry source add --priority <invalid>` fails with a bare `KeyError` instead of a validation message\n### Description\n\n`poetry source add` accepts `--priority` values `primary`, `supplemental` and `explicit`, and its own `--help` lists them, but an invalid value is not validated. The command looks the value up in the `Priority` enum and the resulting `KeyError` reaches the user as the bare string:\n\n```\n$ poetry source add foo https://example.org/simple/ --priority bogus\n'BOGUS'\n```\n\nExit code 1, with no indication of what went wrong or what the valid values are. The same command reports its other two failure modes in plain language (`Source with name ... already exists`, `Source ... is not a valid URL`), so this path is inconsistent with the rest of the command.\n\n### Expected behaviour\n\nSomething like:\n\n```\nInvalid priority 'bogus'. Must be one of: primary, supplemental, explicit.\n```\n\nand exit code 1, like the command's other error paths.\n\n### Notes\n\nThe value is also upper-cased before the lookup, so `--priority=Supplemental` works today and should keep working.\n\nI have a fix with a regression test ready and will open a pull request for it.\n\n", "hints_text": "", "created_at": "2026-10-27T13:54:36Z"}
{"repo": "python-poetry/poetry", "pull_number": 11149, "instance_id": "python-poetry__poetry-11149", "issue_numbers": ["11148"], "base_commit": "d5991b1bc1e5e6a1b23c8bb09745079c45652c52", "patch": "diff --git a/src/poetry/config/config.py b/src/poetry/config/config.py\nindex 8577ad32f22..4334ae01d51 100644\n--- a/src/poetry/config/config.py\n+++ b/src/poetry/config/config.py\n@@ -19,6 +19,7 @@\n from poetry.config.config_source import split_key\n from poetry.config.dict_config_source import DictConfigSource\n from poetry.config.file_config_source import FileConfigSource\n+from poetry.exceptions import PoetryError\n from poetry.locations import CONFIG_DIR\n from poetry.locations import DEFAULT_CACHE_DIR\n from poetry.locations import data_dir\n@@ -406,7 +407,17 @@ def get(self, setting_name: str | Sequence[str], default: Any = None) -> Any:\n                 env = \"POETRY_\" + \"_\".join(k.upper().replace(\"-\", \"_\") for k in keys)\n                 env_value = os.getenv(env)\n                 if env_value is not None:\n-                    return self.process(self.get_normalizer(keys)(env_value))\n+                    normalizer = self.get_normalizer(keys)\n+                    # Integer settings have a validator that can reject the value. Report the\n+                    # environment variable instead of letting int() raise a bare ValueError.\n+                    # Other normalizers coerce unknown values and keep doing so.\n+                    if normalizer is int_normalizer and not self.get_validator(keys)(\n+                        env_value\n+                    ):\n+                        raise PoetryError(\n+                            f\"Invalid value for environment variable {env}: {env_value!r}\"\n+                        )\n+                    return self.process(normalizer(env_value))\n \n         value = self._config\n \n", "test_patch": "diff --git a/tests/config/test_config.py b/tests/config/test_config.py\nindex a7997cc3ce0..61aa268edd8 100644\n--- a/tests/config/test_config.py\n+++ b/tests/config/test_config.py\n@@ -15,6 +15,7 @@\n from poetry.config.config import boolean_normalizer\n from poetry.config.config import int_normalizer\n from poetry.config.config import str_list_normalizer\n+from poetry.exceptions import PoetryError\n from poetry.utils.password_manager import PasswordManager\n from tests.helpers import flatten_dict\n from tests.helpers import isolated_environment\n@@ -148,6 +149,29 @@ def test_config_get_from_environment_variable_nested(\n     assert config.get(\"virtualenvs.options\") == expected\n \n \n+@pytest.mark.parametrize(\n+    (\"name\", \"env_var\", \"env_value\"),\n+    [\n+        (\"requests.max-retries\", \"POETRY_REQUESTS_MAX_RETRIES\", \"not-a-number\"),\n+        (\"installer.max-workers\", \"POETRY_INSTALLER_MAX_WORKERS\", \"not-a-number\"),\n+        (\"solver.min-release-age\", \"POETRY_SOLVER_MIN_RELEASE_AGE\", \"not-a-number\"),\n+        # `installer.max-workers` has minimum 1, matching `poetry config installer.max-workers 0`.\n+        (\"installer.max-workers\", \"POETRY_INSTALLER_MAX_WORKERS\", \"0\"),\n+    ],\n+)\n+def test_config_get_from_environment_variable_invalid_int(\n+    config: Config,\n+    environ: Iterator[None],\n+    name: str,\n+    env_var: str,\n+    env_value: str,\n+) -> None:\n+    os.environ[env_var] = env_value\n+\n+    with pytest.raises(PoetryError, match=env_var):\n+        config.get(name)\n+\n+\n @pytest.mark.parametrize(\n     (\"path_config\", \"expected\"),\n     [(\"~/.venvs\", Path.home() / \".venvs\"), (\"venv\", Path(\"venv\"))],\n", "problem_statement": "config: report the setting name for invalid integer values\n### Description\n\nInvalid values for most settings are reported with a uniform message that names the setting, but values for the three integer settings are not.\n\n### Reproduction\n\n```bash\npoetry config requests.max-retries abc\n```\n\nActual:\n\n```text\ninvalid literal for int() with base 10: 'abc'\n```\n\nExpected (same message as other settings):\n\n```text\n\"abc\" is an invalid value for requests.max-retries\n```\n\nThe same happens for `installer.max-workers` and `solver.min-release-age`, and for the corresponding environment variables (`POETRY_REQUESTS_MAX_RETRIES=abc`).\n\n### Why this is an inconsistency\n\n`ConfigCommand._handle_single_value()` builds the message `\"{value}\" is an invalid value for {key}` for validators that return `False`, and that message is covered by `tests/console/commands/test_config.py`. The three integer validators call `int()` and raise `ValueError` instead of returning `False`, so they bypass this path.\n\n### Impact\n\nThe error does not say which setting is wrong, which is confusing when the value comes from an environment variable or a script.\n\n", "hints_text": "Reopening because only the command line part has been fixed so far.", "created_at": "2026-10-17T18:12:51Z"}
{"repo": "python-poetry/poetry", "pull_number": 11143, "instance_id": "python-poetry__poetry-11143", "issue_numbers": ["4658"], "base_commit": "573926a43b46503b28da07f56db68457bfcd4b77", "patch": "diff --git a/docs/repositories.md b/docs/repositories.md\nindex 2dfbe7274d8..1ffce013d86 100644\n--- a/docs/repositories.md\n+++ b/docs/repositories.md\n@@ -76,6 +76,10 @@ with your team, you can configure the\n poetry config repositories.foo https://pypi.example.org/legacy/\n ```\n \n+The upload URL can differ from the `/simple/` URL used to install packages. Use the upload endpoint\n+documented by your repository provider; `/legacy/` is an example, not a required path for every server.\n+Adding a package source with `poetry source add` does not configure a publishing repository.\n+\n {{% note %}}\n \n If you need to use a different credential for your [package source](#package-sources), then it is\n", "test_patch": "", "problem_statement": "Private PyPi URL for publishing and downloading is not the same\n<!--\r\n  Hi there! Thank you for discovering and submitting an issue with our documentation.\r\n\r\n  Before you submit this; let's make sure of a few things.\r\n  Please make sure the following boxes are ticked if they are correct.\r\n  If not, please try and fulfill these first.\r\n-->\r\n\r\n<!-- Checked checkbox should look like this: [x] -->\r\n- [x] I have searched the [issues](https://github.com/python-poetry/poetry/issues) of this repo and believe that this is not a duplicate.\r\n\r\n## Issue\r\n<!-- Now feel free to write your issue, but please be descriptive! Thanks again \ud83d\ude4c \u2764\ufe0f -->\r\n\r\nHi,\r\n\r\nFirst thank you for your effort on this library.\r\nI have been trying to add a dependency from a private pypi repo and I followed the docs and other internet resources to be able to download and upload the package from/to my private PyPi server. However, after some experiments, I realised that the download and upload just worked using different URLs.\r\n\r\nFor downloading I used the following configuration in `pyproject.toml`, which follows Poetry docs:\r\n```toml\r\n[[tool.poetry.source]]\r\nname = \"foo_api\"\r\nurl = \"https://pypi.foo.com/simple/\"\r\n```\r\nAnd it works perfectly.\r\n\r\nHowever, for uploading I had to use a different URL:\r\n```shell\r\n$ poetry config repo.foo_api https://pypi.foo.com/\r\n$ poetry publish -r foo_api\r\n```\r\nwhich is not what is recommended in the docs [[1]](https://python-poetry.org/docs/repositories/#adding-a-repository)\r\n\r\nIf I use the recommendation from the Docs, then I get the following:\r\n```python\r\nPublishing foo_api (0.1.0) to mqtt_api\r\n - Uploading foo_api-0.1.0-py3-none-any.whl 100%\r\n\r\n  UploadError\r\n\r\n  HTTP Error 405: Method Not Allowed\r\n\r\n  at ~/.virtualenvs/foo_api/lib/python3.10/site-packages/poetry/publishing/uploader.py:216 in _upload\r\n      212\u2502                     self._register(session, url)\r\n      213\u2502                 except HTTPError as e:\r\n      214\u2502                     raise UploadError(e)\r\n      215\u2502\r\n    \u2192 216\u2502             raise UploadError(e)\r\n      217\u2502\r\n      218\u2502     def _do_upload(\r\n      219\u2502         self, session, url, dry_run=False\r\n      220\u2502     ):  # type: (requests.Session, str, Optional[bool]) -> None\r\nmake: *** [deploy] Error 1\r\n```\r\n\r\nSeems I was not the first tumbling into this issue, as I found a similar one in stackoverflow:\r\nhttps://stackoverflow.com/questions/65064910/cant-upload-poetry-package-to-local-dockerized-pypiserver\r\n\r\nInstallation details\r\n`Poetry version 1.1.11`\r\n`Python version 3.10`\r\n`20.6.0 Darwin Kernel Version 20.6.0: Mon Aug 30 06:12:21 PDT 2021; root:xnu-7195.141.6~3/RELEASE_X86_64 x86_64`\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\n", "hints_text": "Similar to Issue: https://github.com/python-poetry/poetry/issues/5348\n@tropxy I suspect you need to identify what upload endpoint to use. \r\n\r\nPoetry distinguishes between sources and repositories for publishing. You are on the correct track, however I suspect `https://pypi.foo.com/` does not accept uploads, the upload url might look like `https://upload.pypi.org/legacy/` ([Warehouse](https://warehouse.pypa.io/api-reference/legacy.html#upload-api)), `https://pkgs.dev.azure.com/<your-organization-name>/<your-project-name>/_packaging/<your-feed-name>/pypi/upload` ([Azure DevOps](https://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/devops/artifacts/quickstarts/python-packages?view=azure-devops)) etc. Might need to chck what your index deployment uses.", "created_at": "2026-10-16T19:28:15Z"}
{"repo": "python-poetry/poetry", "pull_number": 11131, "instance_id": "python-poetry__poetry-11131", "issue_numbers": ["11130"], "base_commit": "906ba21dff6f08c0df7d381a5e7879e12f6102e0", "patch": "diff --git a/src/poetry/installation/chooser.py b/src/poetry/installation/chooser.py\nindex f3d76d41f62..972cafde43f 100644\n--- a/src/poetry/installation/chooser.py\n+++ b/src/poetry/installation/chooser.py\n@@ -217,13 +217,15 @@ def _choose_hash_verified_link(\n             links, key=lambda link: self._sort_key(package, link), reverse=True\n         )\n \n-        locked_hashes = {f[\"hash\"] for f in package.files}\n-        if not locked_hashes:\n+        if not package.files:\n             return ordered_links[0]\n \n         skipped = []\n-        locked_hash_names = {h.split(\":\")[0] for h in locked_hashes}\n         for link in ordered_links:\n+            locked_hashes = {\n+                f[\"hash\"] for f in package.files if f[\"file\"] == link.filename\n+            }\n+            locked_hash_names = {h.split(\":\")[0] for h in locked_hashes}\n             # A link that advertises no hash is not trusted: the lock file requires\n             # a hash for this package, so fall through and compute one to compare.\n             link_hash: str | None = None\n@@ -231,7 +233,6 @@ def _choose_hash_verified_link(\n                 hash_name := get_highest_priority_hash_type(candidates, link.filename)\n             ):\n                 link_hash = f\"{hash_name}:{link.hashes[hash_name]}\"\n-\n             elif isinstance(repository, HTTPRepository):\n                 link_hash = repository.calculate_sha256(link)\n \n@@ -247,7 +248,7 @@ def _choose_hash_verified_link(\n \n         reason = f\"Downloaded distributions for <b>{package.pretty_name} ({package.pretty_version})</> did not match any known checksums in your lock file.\"\n         link_hashes = \"\\n\".join(f\"  - {link}({h})\" for link, h in skipped)\n-        known_hashes = \"\\n\".join(f\"  - {h}\" for h in locked_hashes)\n+        known_hashes = \"\\n\".join(f\"  - {f['hash']}\" for f in package.files)\n         messages = [\n             ConsoleMessage(\n                 \"<options=bold>Causes:</>\\n\"\n", "test_patch": "diff --git a/tests/installation/test_chooser.py b/tests/installation/test_chooser.py\nindex f9767ac6eba..ec564a51ebc 100644\n--- a/tests/installation/test_chooser.py\n+++ b/tests/installation/test_chooser.py\n@@ -379,6 +379,140 @@ def test_chooser_accepts_a_hashless_link_whose_computed_hash_matches(\n     assert link.filename == \"isort-4.3.4.tar.gz\"\n \n \n+def test_chooser_accepts_matching_file_hash_when_lock_mixes_algorithms(\n+    env: MockEnv, pool: RepositoryPool, mocker: MockerFixture\n+) -> None:\n+    \"\"\"A PEP 691 index may list several hashes per file. If the lock entry for\n+    the package mixes algorithms (one file sha256, another sha512), a file is\n+    still valid when its advertised sha256 matches the locked hash for that file.\n+    \"\"\"\n+    sha256_wheel = \"sha256:\" + \"a\" * 64\n+    sha512_sdist = \"sha512:\" + \"b\" * 128\n+    other_sha512 = \"c\" * 128\n+\n+    package = Package(\n+        \"markupsafe\",\n+        \"3.0.1\",\n+        source_type=\"legacy\",\n+        source_reference=\"foo\",\n+        source_url=\"https://legacy.foo.bar/simple/\",\n+    )\n+    package.files = [\n+        {\"file\": \"MarkupSafe-3.0.1-py3-none-any.whl\", \"hash\": sha256_wheel},\n+        {\"file\": \"markupsafe-3.0.1.tar.gz\", \"hash\": sha512_sdist},\n+    ]\n+\n+    wheel = Link(\n+        \"https://legacy.foo.bar/MarkupSafe-3.0.1-py3-none-any.whl\",\n+        hashes={\"sha256\": \"a\" * 64, \"sha512\": other_sha512},\n+    )\n+    sdist = Link(\n+        \"https://legacy.foo.bar/markupsafe-3.0.1.tar.gz\",\n+        hashes={\"sha512\": \"b\" * 128},\n+    )\n+\n+    mocker.patch.object(\n+        LegacyRepository, \"find_links_for_package\", return_value=[wheel, sdist]\n+    )\n+    calculate_sha256 = mocker.patch.object(LegacyRepository, \"calculate_sha256\")\n+\n+    link = Chooser(pool, env).choose_for(package)\n+\n+    assert link.filename == \"MarkupSafe-3.0.1-py3-none-any.whl\"\n+    calculate_sha256.assert_not_called()\n+\n+\n+def test_chooser_rejects_when_no_advertised_hash_matches_mixed_lock(\n+    env: MockEnv, pool: RepositoryPool, mocker: MockerFixture\n+) -> None:\n+    \"\"\"Mixed lock algorithms must not accept a file whose advertised hashes\n+    are all unknown, even when a higher-priority algorithm is present.\n+    \"\"\"\n+    package = Package(\n+        \"markupsafe\",\n+        \"3.0.1\",\n+        source_type=\"legacy\",\n+        source_reference=\"foo\",\n+        source_url=\"https://legacy.foo.bar/simple/\",\n+    )\n+    package.files = [\n+        {\"file\": \"MarkupSafe-3.0.1-py3-none-any.whl\", \"hash\": \"sha256:\" + \"a\" * 64},\n+        {\"file\": \"markupsafe-3.0.1.tar.gz\", \"hash\": \"sha512:\" + \"b\" * 128},\n+    ]\n+\n+    wheel = Link(\n+        \"https://legacy.foo.bar/MarkupSafe-3.0.1-py3-none-any.whl\",\n+        hashes={\"sha256\": \"d\" * 64, \"sha512\": \"e\" * 128},\n+    )\n+\n+    mocker.patch.object(\n+        LegacyRepository, \"find_links_for_package\", return_value=[wheel]\n+    )\n+\n+    with pytest.raises(PoetryRuntimeError) as e:\n+        Chooser(pool, env).choose_for(package)\n+\n+    assert \"did not match any known checksums\" in str(e.value)\n+    # The other file's locked algorithm must not affect this wheel's hash check.\n+    assert \"sha256:\" + \"d\" * 64 in e.value.get_text(debug=True, strip=True)\n+\n+\n+@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"sha512_matches\", [False, True])\n+def test_chooser_checks_highest_priority_hash_for_the_file(\n+    env: MockEnv,\n+    pool: RepositoryPool,\n+    mocker: MockerFixture,\n+    sha512_matches: bool,\n+) -> None:\n+    package = Package(\n+        \"markupsafe\", \"3.0.1\", source_type=\"legacy\", source_reference=\"foo\"\n+    )\n+    filename = \"MarkupSafe-3.0.1-py3-none-any.whl\"\n+    package.files = [\n+        {\"file\": filename, \"hash\": \"sha256:\" + \"a\" * 64},\n+        {\"file\": filename, \"hash\": \"sha512:\" + \"b\" * 128},\n+    ]\n+    wheel = Link(\n+        f\"https://legacy.foo.bar/{filename}\",\n+        hashes={\"sha256\": \"a\" * 64, \"sha512\": (\"b\" if sha512_matches else \"c\") * 128},\n+    )\n+    mocker.patch.object(\n+        LegacyRepository, \"find_links_for_package\", return_value=[wheel]\n+    )\n+    calculate_sha256 = mocker.patch.object(LegacyRepository, \"calculate_sha256\")\n+\n+    if sha512_matches:\n+        assert Chooser(pool, env).choose_for(package) == wheel\n+    else:\n+        with pytest.raises(PoetryRuntimeError):\n+            Chooser(pool, env).choose_for(package)\n+    calculate_sha256.assert_not_called()\n+\n+\n+def test_chooser_rejects_a_hash_locked_for_a_different_file(\n+    env: MockEnv, pool: RepositoryPool, mocker: MockerFixture\n+) -> None:\n+    package = Package(\n+        \"markupsafe\", \"3.0.1\", source_type=\"legacy\", source_reference=\"foo\"\n+    )\n+    package.files = [\n+        {\"file\": \"MarkupSafe-3.0.1-py3-none-any.whl\", \"hash\": \"sha256:\" + \"a\" * 64},\n+        {\"file\": \"markupsafe-3.0.1.tar.gz\", \"hash\": \"sha256:\" + \"b\" * 64},\n+    ]\n+    wheel = Link(\n+        \"https://legacy.foo.bar/MarkupSafe-3.0.1-py3-none-any.whl\",\n+        hashes={\"sha256\": \"b\" * 64},\n+    )\n+    mocker.patch.object(\n+        LegacyRepository, \"find_links_for_package\", return_value=[wheel]\n+    )\n+    calculate_sha256 = mocker.patch.object(LegacyRepository, \"calculate_sha256\")\n+\n+    with pytest.raises(PoetryRuntimeError):\n+        Chooser(pool, env).choose_for(package)\n+    calculate_sha256.assert_not_called()\n+\n+\n def test_chooser_stops_checking_hashes_once_a_candidate_matches(\n     env: MockEnv, pool: RepositoryPool, mocker: MockerFixture\n ) -> None:\n", "problem_statement": "poetry install skips valid files when a package's lock entry mixes sha256 and sha512 (JSON index)\n### Description\n\n## Summary\n\nWhen a package index's JSON simple API (PEP 691) lists several hashes for a file, and the package's lock entry contains hashes of more than one algorithm, `poetry install` rejects files even though one of their listed hashes exactly matches the hash locked for that file.\n\nThe rejected files are skipped with only a debug log line. If the sdist still matches, Poetry silently builds from source instead of using the wheel. Once no installable file is left, the install fails with;\n\n- 2.4.x: `Unable to find installation candidates for markupsafe (3.0.0)` /\n  `59 wheel(s) were skipped as your project's environment does not support the identified abi tags`\n\n- 2.5.x: `Downloaded distributions for markupsafe (3.0.0) did not match any known checksums in your lock file.`\n\nI believe that this bug has been present from `2.3.0` and above, when Poetry was changed to prefer JSON over HTML indexes for legacy and private repositories. The error differs between versions, but the underlying cause is the same.\n\nIf any of the distributions for the desired version of a package present a `sha512` hash, this will then be selected from the JSON index hash array to match against the lockfile, and the `sha256` hash will be discarded. As a result of this, packages that are presenting a valid `sha256` hash from the JSON index are then ignored, despite the hash presented matching the hash in the lockfile.\n\n## Context\n\nWe are consuming packages from a local PyPI mirror using a product called ProGet (built by Inedo) - ProGet is configured in our environment to use lazy caching, where we are mirroring pypi.org public packages, but only caching a specific distribution locally after the first install. \n\nThis bug has to light due to the way ProGet handles algorithms for cached vs uncached packages, where the JSON index will present a `sha256` hash only for uncached packages (which will make its way into the poetry lockfile if this is the first timing consuming a new distribution), and an array of hashes (sha256, sha512, md1, md5) for distributions that have been cached. \n\nA similar bug was present (and fixed) in `uv`, \nhttps://github.com/astral-sh/uv/issues/17143\n\nWhilst we agree that presenting a different set of hashes for cached vs uncached packages via the JSON index is peculiar behaviour on the ProGet side, it does still conform with PEP 691, as there is nothing in the spec against this. \n\nThis is mostly an interoperability issue between the two products, but I believe the core bug here is that Poetry makes an assumption that the PEP spec does not guarantee - that the type of hashing algorithms presented in the JSON index will not change between lock and install of packages.\n\n### Workarounds\n\nRe-running a `poetry lock` will modify the failed package in the lockfile from a `sha256` hash to a `sha512` hash, which will resolve the issue until pumping. \n\n### Poetry Installation Method\n\ninstall.python-poetry.org\n\n### Operating System\n\nDebian 12\n\n### Poetry Version\n\n2.5.1\n\n### Poetry Configuration\n\n```bash session\ncache-dir = \"/root/.cache/pypoetry\"\ndata-dir = \"/root/.local/share/pypoetry\"\ninstaller.builtin-uninstall = false\ninstaller.max-workers = null\ninstaller.no-binary = null\ninstaller.only-binary = null\ninstaller.parallel = true\ninstaller.re-resolve = false\nkeyring.enabled = true\npython.installation-dir = \"{data-dir}/python\"  # /root/.local/share/pypoetry/python\nrepositories.public-pypi.url = \"https://{__MASKED_INTERNAL_DOMAIN__}/pypi/public-pypi/simple\"\nrequests.max-retries = 0\nsolver.lazy-wheel = true\nsolver.min-release-age = 0\nsolver.min-release-age-exclude = null\nsolver.min-release-age-exclude-source = null\nsystem-git-client = false\nvirtualenvs.create = true\nvirtualenvs.in-project = null\nvirtualenvs.options.always-copy = false\nvirtualenvs.options.no-pip = false\nvirtualenvs.options.system-site-packages = false\nvirtualenvs.path = \"{cache-dir}/virtualenvs\"  # /root/.cache/pypoetry/virtualenvs\nvirtualenvs.prompt = \"{project_name}-py{python_version}\"\nvirtualenvs.use-poetry-python = false\n```\n\n### Python Sysconfig\n\n_No response_\n\n### Example pyproject.toml\n\n```TOML\n\n```\n\n### Poetry Runtime Logs\n\n<details>\n  <summary>poetry-runtime.log</summary>\n  <!-- Please leave one blank line below for enabling the code block rendering. -->\n\n  ```\nAdding repository public-pypi (https://{__MASKED_INTERNAL_DOMAIN__}/pypi/public-pypi/simple) and setting it as primary\nDeactivating the PyPI repository\n[findpython:findpython] Running script: ['/usr/local/bin/python', '-Ic', 'import sys; print(sys.executable)']\nFound: /usr/local/bin/python\n[findpython:findpython] Running script: ['/usr/local/bin/python', '-Ic', 'import platform; print(platform.python_version())']\nFound: /usr/local/bin/python\nCreating virtualenv hash-repro-DJpFP61h-py3.12 in /root/.cache/pypoetry/virtualenvs\n[virtualenv:virtualenv.app_data] created app data folder /root/.cache/virtualenv\n[python_discovery:python_discovery._discovery] find interpreter for spec PythonSpec(path=/usr/local/bin/python3.12)\n[python_discovery:python_discovery._compat] filesystem is case-sensitive\n[python_discovery:python_discovery._discovery] proposed PythonInfo(spec=CPython3.12.13.final.0-64-x86_64, exe=/usr/local/bin/python3.12, platform=linux, version='3.12.13 (main, Aug  5 2026, 01:10:24) [GCC 14.2.0]', encoding_fs_io=utf-8-utf-8)\n[python_discovery:python_discovery._discovery] accepted PythonInfo(spec=CPython3.12.13.final.0-64-x86_64, exe=/usr/local/bin/python3.12, platform=linux, version='3.12.13 (main, Aug  5 2026, 01:10:24) [GCC 14.2.0]', encoding_fs_io=utf-8-utf-8)\n[virtualenv:virtualenv.info] symlink on filesystem does work\n[virtualenv:virtualenv.info] filesystem is case-sensitive\n[virtualenv:virtualenv.seed.embed.base_embed] DEPRECATION: the --wheel and --no-wheel options do nothing; virtualenv no longer bundles wheel. T